      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Given that the pressure of a gas is inversely proportional to its volume at constant temperature, we can find the new pressure using the formula for inverse proportionality.\n∵ P1V1 = P2V2\n\nP1 is the initial pressure = 5 kPa\nV1 is the initial volume = 2.28 liters\n\nP2 is the final pressure = ?\nV2 is the final volume = 5.7 liters\n\nPlugging in the given values, we have:\n\n5 kPa * 2.28 liters = P2 * 5.7 liters\n\nTo solve for P2, divide both sides by 5.7 liters:\n\nP2 = (5 kPa * 2.28 liters) / 5.7 liters\n\nP2 = 2.28 kPa\n\nso, P2 is the final pressure which is 2.28 kPa.\nThe answer is: 2.28",
