    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We are given that the pressure \\( P \\) is inversely proportional to the volume \\( V \\) at constant temperature. This means that the product of pressure and volume remains constant:\n\\[ P \\times V = k \\]\nwhere \\( k \\) is the constant of proportionality.\n\nInitially, we have:\n- Volume \\( V_1 = 2.28 \\) liters\n- Pressure \\( P_1 = 5 \\) kPa\n\nUsing the constant of proportionality \\( k \\):\n\\[ P_1 \\times V_1 = k \\]\n\\[ k = P_1 \\times V_1 = 5 \\times 2.28 \\]\n\nNow, if we move the oxygen to a 5.7 liter container:\n- Volume \\( V_2 = 5.7 \\) liters\n- We need to find the new pressure \\( P_2 \\).\n\nUsing the constant \\( k \\) again:\n\\[ P_2 \\times V_2 = k \\]\n\\[ P_2 \\times 5.7 = 5 \\times 2.28 \\]\n\nSolve for \\( P_2 \\):\n\\[ P_2 = \\frac{5 \\times 2.28}{5.7} \\]\n\\[ P_2 = \\frac{11.4}{5.7} \\approx 2 \\text{ kPa} \\]\n\nThus, the new pressure is approximately \\(\\boxed{2}\\) kPa.",
